        "title": "Ancient and Medieval Historians",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The historians of antiquity and the medieval period invented the fundamental conventions that Western and Islamic historiography still operate within: the question of evidence (what sources do you trust, and why?), the question of causation (why did events happen?), and the question of purpose (is history a guide to action, a record of memory, or a moral exemplar?). The answers differed radically between authors."
